 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "TemporalKVStore() starts empty. set(key, value, timestamp) stores value for key at timestamp; timestamps passed to set and remove never decrease over the whole call sequence, and a set at the same timestamp as the key's latest version replaces that version. get(key, timestamp) returns the value of the key's latest version with version time <= timestamp, or \"\" when there is none (get timestamps may be any value). remove(key, timestamp) records a deletion version at timestamp (same replacement rule as set): a later get at or after that time, and before the next set, returns \"\". It returns true when get(key, timestamp) would have returned a non-empty value just before the call. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
    "sha256": "be5d798382a43847401e76609d79932746e664be0d91c81b132bf6b46cd69126",
    "selector": "/problems/2/inferred_spec"
   }
  ]
 },
 "contentScope": "authored",
